  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water footprint analysis</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Egypt possesses a diverse horticultural sector that plays a significant economic role within the country. The agriculture sector is responsible for approximately 80% of water consumption. Furthermore, Egypt is impacted by climate change, resulting in a.o. increased water and soil salinity levels.RVO and the Netherlands embassy in Cairo, Egypt, are commissioning a water footprint study that supports Dutch and Egyptian agriculture entrepreneurs in increasing their environmental sustainability and climate resiliency by reducing the water footprint of selected agricultural products (indicator crops).The study serves two goals:1.	Understanding the water footprint of various (indicator) crops that Egypt exports to the Netherlands, and2.	identification of opportunities for NL businesses to support Egyptian farmers in reducing their water footprint.</narrative>
  </description>
